# CAN v2 fleet sweep — findings, decisions and what is still UNPROVEN [SPEC:CANV2-SWEEP]

> A wholesale CAN-v2 conversion was dispatched across "the entire fleet". The conversion was
> already complete before this session began, because THE FLEET HAS EXACTLY ONE CONVERTIBLE CAN
> PEER and it was converted on 2026-08-14. What the sweep actually produced is a roster
> correction, four remediations, two measurements that settle ratified disagreements, the
> identification of the `0xDEAD` constant, and — the most valuable result — the FIRST MEASURED
> CROSS-SILICON v2 INTEROP on real wire. No ESP32 flash was written in this session.

- document-status: WORKING DOCUMENT for architect review. NOT a canonical corpus file. It is deliberately in `docs/` rather than `corpora/platform-specs/` because `docs/` is not a registered corpus root, so landing it mutates no live graph. Promote deliberately or not at all.
- sweep-date: 2026-08-15
- authored-by: composeio-hardware-architect subagent, dispatched with authority to flash, deploy and make reasonable technical calls, architect reviewing after.
- evidence-discipline: every claim below is tagged MEASURED, INFERENCE or DATASHEET. Per [CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS], a machine signal that agrees with the wrong answer is the failure mode being designed against, so every wire claim here was read back through an instrument INDEPENDENT of the thing that wrote it.
- flash-writes-this-session: NONE. No ESP32 firmware was written, so no factory-image backup was required. The only writes were three Raspberry Pi config files, all backed up with SHA-256 before the first change — see [CANV2-REVERSAL].
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-VISION], [CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS], [BP-CAN-ID], [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], [SPEC:CXC-BOARD-HW]

