## The roster is NOT what the dispatch assumed — one convertible peer, not a fleet [CANV2-ROSTER]

- headline: MEASURED — the fleet contains exactly THREE CAN-relevant nodes, not a fleet of them. Two are ESP32s on USB and one is the Pi. Of the two ESP32s, one is the ring-fenced controller that is not a CAN peer at all, and the other was already converted. There was no wholesale conversion left to perform.
- node-cio-ctrl-db1c: MEASURED — USB serial `00:00:5E:00:53:02`, mapped PASSIVELY to `/dev/cu.usbmodem31101`. NEVER TOUCHED, as instructed. It reaches the bridge over MQTT and puts no frames on CAN, so it needs no conversion. Confirmed from the bridge's own logs, which show `throttle/right` arriving MQTT-side with `src=cio-ctrl-db1c`.
- node-c3lcd-047dd8: MEASURED — USB serial `00:00:5E:00:53:03`, mapped PASSIVELY to `/dev/cu.usbmodem11301`. Already on v2. Its boot banner states the layout in full: `[BP-CAN-ID] v2 prio(3)|type(4)|ns(16)|src(4)|scope(2)`.
- node-rpi5: MEASURED — `display-node.local`, two MCP2515 channels (`mcp251x` on `spi0.0`/`spi0.1`) plus `composeio-can-bridge.service`. NOT rebooted at any point; only individual services were restarted.
- identity-method: MEASURED — port-to-serial mapping was resolved by walking the `ioreg` USB tree to the `IOCalloutDevice` leaf, which reads the descriptor and RESETS NOTHING. `esptool chip-id` was never used; it resets the board, which is the exact harm the check exists to prevent.
- the-two-c3s-share-a-prefix: Both ESP32s are `1C:DB:D4:xx:xx:xx`. Only the FULL serial separates the ring-fenced controller from the board that was worked on. Every operation in this session was aimed at `/dev/cu.usbmodem11301` only.
- devices-that-do-not-exist-physically: INFERENCE — the firmware tree carries CAN build envs for a headless relay (`esp32_can_relay`), a pin-drive test, a CAN filter bench, and the corpus describes a CH32V003 + MCP2515 gateway PCB ([PCB-CANGW]). NONE of these is physically present. They are designs and bench tools, not unconverted nodes.
- fourth-usb-device-unidentified: EMPTY — an FTDI `USB <-> Serial Cable`, serial `<device-serial>`, is attached at `/dev/cu.usbserial-<device-serial>`. What is on the far end is UNKNOWN and was deliberately NOT probed: opening an FTDI port asserts DTR/RTS and can reset whatever is attached, and nothing identified it as a CAN node. NEEDS DAVID'S EYES.
- mqtt-census-is-empty-of-devices: MEASURED — a 25-second subscription to `composeio/#` on the broker returned 58 topics and ZERO `_device/*` topics. No embedded node is announcing on MQTT. The live topics are software intelligences and a kiosk.
- part-of: [SPEC:CANV2-SWEEP]

