## restart-ms was deliberately LEFT AT 100 — half a ratified decision is worse than none [CANV2-RESTART-MS]

- ratified-preference: `restart-ms 0` with counted, logged recovery, in place of the current `restart-ms 100`.
- decision: NOT APPLIED. `restart-ms 100` is retained on both interfaces.
- reasoning: The ratified decision has two halves — remove the blind auto-restart, AND add counted, logged recovery in its place. The second half DOES NOT EXIST in any code on this host. Applying only the first half would remove the safety net without adding the instrument, so a real bus-off would leave the interface down indefinitely with nothing recording it.
- and-it-buys-nothing-today: [CANV2-BUSOFF-EXPERIMENT] measured that the Pi does not reach bus-off in its dominant fault mode, so the auto-restart being removed is inert anyway. All risk, no benefit, until the counter exists.
- how-to-reverse-this-non-change: If the architect wants it anyway, it is one word in each of `/etc/systemd/system/can0.service` and `can1.service`. It is a non-change, recorded so that "nobody thought of it" and "it was considered and declined" are distinguishable.
- part-of: [SPEC:CANV2-SWEEP]

