## 0xDEAD identified — a hand-built synthetic frame, not a fleet device [CANV2-DEAD-CONSTANT]

- the-question: The retired v1 bridge's final census reported 84,965 frames dropped as unresolvable, 84,961 of them namespace hash `0xDEAD`. A deliberate-looking constant is not noise.
- measured-identity: Recovered from journald, which outlived the wiped registry file. EVERY such frame carried CAN id `0x1BD5BE00` with exactly 8 data bytes.
- the-decode: `0x1BD5BE00 >> 13 = 57005 = 0xDEAD` EXACTLY. Under the v1 layout `ns_hash(16) | type(4) | src(9)` that is `ns=0xDEAD`, `type=15`, `src=0`. Type 15 is the maximum representable 4-bit type code.
- why-it-is-synthetic: INFERENCE, strong. The id is not the CRC-16 of any namespace — every plausible fleet namespace was hashed and none produces `0xDEAD`. It is a hand-chosen memorable constant, shifted into the v1 namespace field, carrying an out-of-range type and a maximal payload. That is a frame built BY HAND to be unresolvable.
- most-likely-purpose: INFERENCE, not proven. It has the exact shape of a NEGATIVE CONTROL for the bridge's unresolvable-drop census — the deliberate fault injector that [CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS] `rule-negative-control` demands, without which a drop counter reading zero means nothing. `cangen` is the documented injection tool on this bench and is recorded in `docs/board-bringup/esp32c3-supermini-can.md` injecting a fixed id on `can1`. The human INTENT is not proven and is not claimed.
- the-other-two-hashes-are-also-explained: MEASURED. The same census listed `0x254C` x3 and `0x443A` x1. The c3lcd boot banner names both: `0x254C` is `_device/c3lcd-047dd8/transport` and `0x443A` is `_device/c3lcd-047dd8/config_source`. Those are control commands aimed at the board over CAN, unresolvable at the bridge only because its hand-typed register list names the OTHER firmware's device prefix — see [CANV2-REGISTER-UNMADE].
- is-it-still-happening: MEASURED — NO. Two independent watches, 15 s and 30 s, across BOTH channels, captured ZERO frames. No `cangen`, `cansend` or `canplayer` process is running, there is no cron entry and no systemd timer. The emitter is gone.
- residual-risk: If it recurs it will be a person at a keyboard, not a device. Nothing needs to be defended against.
- part-of: [SPEC:CANV2-SWEEP]

