## What I could NOT verify — explicit EMPTY slots [CANV2-UNPROVEN]

- esp32-transmit-onto-the-segment: EMPTY. Blocked by the dead transceiver driver. No software instrument on this bench can see past it, and a listen-only node is invisible on the wire by construction.
- whether-a-replacement-transceiver-is-fitted: EMPTY. Requires physical inspection or a meter across CANH/CANL. NEEDS DAVID'S EYES.
- the-ftdi-cable-far-end: EMPTY. Serial `<device-serial>`. Not probed, deliberately — opening an FTDI port asserts DTR/RTS and may reset whatever is attached. Its far end is unidentified. NEEDS DAVID'S EYES.
- sample-point-mismatch-under-load: EMPTY. Pi at 87.5% and ESP32 at 80% is within tolerance by calculation, but has never been exercised with the ESP32 actually transmitting, because it cannot. Unfalsifiable until the transceiver is fixed.
- the-dead-constant-author-intent: EMPTY. `0xDEAD` — the frame's identity and syntheticity are measured; the human purpose is inferred from shape and remains unproven.
- bus-off-recovery-behaviour-on-the-esp32: EMPTY. The banner asserts no auto-recovery and no `twai_initiate_recovery()` call; this session did not exercise it, since the node cannot transmit.
- negative-control-for-this-session-s-interop-test: PARTIAL. The interop proof has a natural negative control — before the bridge restart the board logged nothing on that namespace, and after it logged the receive. But no deliberate WRONG-format frame was injected to confirm the board would REJECT it. The v2-decodes-v1 silent-drop failure mode is therefore still only argued, not demonstrated, on this hardware.
- part-of: [SPEC:CANV2-SWEEP]

