## How to reverse every change in this session [CANV2-REVERSAL]

- scope-of-changes: THREE Raspberry Pi config files and ONE repository file. No ESP32 flash was written. No device was rebooted. `display-node.local` was NOT rebooted; only `composeio-can-bridge`, `can0` and `can1` were restarted.
- backups: All three host files were copied to `/var/backups/can-v2-sweep-20260815/` BEFORE the first write, with SHA-256 recorded: `can0.service` = `5de22cf981e29d6371af920793da4331a82f93661ab513305c0652edaba12c52`, `can1.service` = `d50782b9f0234769065923bbae83d6026ff053957b730618ab9b2508740e8323`, `composeio-can-bridge` = `e4d740260a3bbc15d73939c96b74520dcd9ca6264e715f6bc27f45bd4ad21984`.
- reverse-the-node-id: Remove or set to 0 the `CAN_BRIDGE_NODE_ID` line in `/etc/default/composeio-can-bridge`, and revert the corresponding block in `deploy/can_mqtt_bridge/composeio-can-bridge.env`, then restart the bridge. Reverting only the host file will be undone by the next deploy.
- reverse-the-sjw: Restore `can0.service` and `can1.service` from the backup directory, `systemctl daemon-reload`, then bring both interfaces down and up. The pre-change ExecStart had no `sjw` argument, which is the driver default of 1.
- transient-states-already-restored: The bus-off experiment took `can1` down and set `can0` to `restart-ms 0`. Both were restored in the same script via an EXIT trap, and the restoration was verified by read-back: both interfaces are ERROR-ACTIVE with `restart-ms 100` and `sjw 2`, and the bridge is active.
- the-board-was-reset-not-flashed: `c3lcd-047dd8` was reset twice via a DTR/RTS pulse to read its boot banner. It booted normally each time — `rst:0x15 (USB_UART_CHIP_RESET), boot:0xd (SPI_FAST_FLASH_BOOT)` — and never entered download mode. Its flash is byte-identical to what it held before this session.
- running-build-confirmed-by-compiler-written-markers: `App version: 1b72183-dirty`, `Compile time: Aug 14 2026 10:55:09`, `ESP-IDF 5.5.2.260206`, `Device id: c3lcd-047dd8`. These are `__DATE__`/`__TIME__` and a git-describe stamp, not a hand-maintained tag — the class of marker that read `TF13` through ten flashes in this fleet's history.
- part-of: [SPEC:CANV2-SWEEP]
